# The Dockerfile ends with `COPY . /app/`, so anything not excluded here is baked
# into a published image.
#
# This file exists because Trivy caught the pipeline poisoning its own artifact:
# after a local `make scan`, the build copied reports/.gitleaks-unredacted.json -
# a file of plaintext secrets - into the image, which CI then pushes to GHCR. The
# scanner output became part of the shipped attack surface. It also inflated the
# image and the SBOM with thousands of cache files.
#
# Rule of thumb: if it is generated, secret, or only useful to a developer, it has
# no business in a runtime image.

# --- Version control and CI ---
.git
.gitignore
.github
.gitleaks.toml
.yamllint.yml

# --- Generated scanner output: NEVER in an image ---
reports/
sbom/
.cache/
.trivycache/
.semgrep/
*.sarif
*-report.json

# --- Security tooling and policy (evaluated in CI, not needed at runtime) ---
.security/
policy/
Makefile

# --- Deployment manifests (applied to a cluster, not shipped inside the app) ---
deploy/

# --- Local developer noise ---
.vscode/
.claude/
.gstack/
diagrams/
venv/
env/
.env
*.pyc
__pycache__/
*.sqlite3
*db.sqlite3*
app.log
test.log

# --- Docs: keep the image lean; they are on GitHub ---
docs/
README.md
*.md
